{%- comment -%}
	Single source of truth for the accepted line-item/note-attribute property
	names for the customer's chosen date, current name first (the first entry
	is what NEW orders get written under; the rest are old aliases kept only
	so past orders still resolve).

	Read by:
	- layout/theme.liquid (renders this once in <head> into window.DELIVERY_DATE_PROPERTY_NAMES
	  / window.DELIVERY_DATE_PROPERTY_KEY, which every write site — theme.liquid,
	  product-template.liquid, header.liquid, wholesaler-shared.js — uses instead
	  of a hardcoded string)
	- snippets/account-order-row.liquid and sections/account-template.liquid
	  (Liquid read sites, for old-order fallback)

	Liquid usage:
		{%- capture delivery_date_property_names_str -%}
			{%- render 'delivery-date-property-names' -%}
		{%- endcapture -%}
		{%- assign delivery_date_property_names = delivery_date_property_names_str | strip | split: ',' -%}
		{%- for name in delivery_date_property_names -%} ... {%- endfor -%}

	Casing matters here: every read site compares EXACTLY (Liquid
	'property.first == property_name'), and the first entry is written verbatim
	as the cart property key, so these must match the customer-facing key
	character for character. Keep them comma-separated with no spaces around
	the commas and no trailing newline.

	Note the reader repos that match case-insensitively (pharmacor-cronjob-app,
	pharmacor-hubspot-project, pharmacor-checkout-extension) keep their own
	lists LOWERCASED; custom-subscription's list matches this file's casing.

	RENAME-DELIVERY-DATE-HERE: add the new name to the FRONT of the list below
	(new,old,older,...) — nothing else anywhere in the theme needs to change.
{%- endcomment -%}Processed Date,Delivery Date